<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kazakh–Dzungar wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1643">1643</a>–<a href="/years/1756">1756</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kazakh–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a> wars were a series of conflicts from the 1640s to the 1750s between the Kazakh Khanate and the Dzungar Khanate for the steppes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. The Dzungar invasion of 1723, remembered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakhs</a> as the 'Years of Great Disaster', drove many Kazakhs from their lands; the wars ended when the Qing destroyed the Dzungar state in the 1750s.</p></div>
